[% INCLUDE start.en %]

<section class="doc-section">
	<h2>GraphQL Builder</h2>
	<div class="section-block">
<ul>
<li>
Select a component and a field. In most cases, the field is the <strong>ID</strong>
of the component. They are called <strong>Primary Component</strong> and <strong>Primary Key</strong>.
<li>
Select a <strong>Foreign Component</strong> and a <strong>Foreign
Key</strong>, which is linked to the <strong>Primary Key</strong>.
</ul>
<p>
Then if you request the <strong>Primary Component</strong> in GraphQL,
you have option to retrieve the <strong>Foreign Component</strong> objects, as <em>List</em>, using the associated key pair.
</p>

<div class="table-responsive">
<table class="table table-striped">
	<thead class="thead-light">
<tr>
<th rowspan=2>Object Name</th>
<th colspan=2>Primary</th>
<th colspan=2>Foreign</th>
<th rowspan=2></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<th>Component</th>
<th>Key</th>
<th>Component</th>
<th>Key</th>
</tr>
</thead>

<tbody>[% FOREACH item IN topics %]
<tr>
<td>[% item.object_name %]</td>
<td>[% item.name_component %]</td>
<td>[% item.object_key %]</td>
<td>[% item.othername %]</td>
<td>[% item.otherfk %]</td>
<td><a class="btn btn-sm btn-warning" href="nextpage?nextpageid=[% item.nextpageid %]&action=delete&projectid=[% projectid %]&projectmd5=[% projectmd5 %]&componentid=[% item.componentid %]&componentmd5=[% item.componentmd5 %]">DEL</a></td>
</tr>[% END %]
<tr><td colspan=6><h5>Add a New GraphQL Object:</h5></td></tr>
<tr><form class="form-inline" method=post action="nextpage">
<input type=hidden name="action" value="insert">
<input type=hidden name="projectid" value="[% projectid %]">
<input type=hidden name="projectmd5" value="[% projectmd5 %]">
<td><input type=text class="form-control input-sm" name="object_name" placeholder="choose a name"></td>
<td><select name=componentid class="form-control" id="componentid"><option value="">-- SELECT --</option>[% FOREACH c=component_topics %]
<option value="[% c.componentid %]">[% c.name_component %]</option>
[% END %]</select>
</td>

<td><select name=object_key class="form-control" id="object_key"><option value="">-- SELECT --</option></select>
</td>

<td><select name=otherid class="form-control" id="otherid"><option value="">-- SELECT --</option>[% FOREACH c=component_topics %]
<option value="[% c.componentid %]">[% c.name_component %]</option>
[% END %]</select>
</td>

<td><select name=otherfk class="form-control" id="otherfk"><option value="">-- SELECT --</option></select>
</td>

<td><button class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" type=submit>Add</button></td></form>
</tr>

</tbody>
</table>
</div>

	</div>
</section>

<section class="doc-section">
	<h2>Remarks</h2>
	<div class="section-block">
<h5>Access Control List</h5>
<p>
Just because a foriegn component is associated, 
doesn't mean the client can always get it.
Querying the foreign component is automatically subject to role's 
access right on the <em>List</em> action.
</p>
<h5>Chain of Queries</h5>
<p>
If the ACL allows, client can query foreign components in a chain till the last component.
</p>
<h5>No 1-to-1 Relationship</h5>
<p>
If only one foreign object be returned from the association, 
which is sometimes called <em>1-to-1 relationship</em>, you would be
strongly recommeneded to use the <em>Join Multiple Tables</em> solution. 
Querying an <em>1-to-1 relationship</em> object is still fine, but less
efficient than using <em>Join</em>.
</p>

    </div>
</section>

[% INCLUDE end.en %]
